---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleList from '../components/ArticleList.astro';
import ProjectList from '../components/ProjectList.astro';
import writing from '../data/writing.json';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="introduction">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Science, writing & things in progress</p>
        <h1 id="introduction">Anthony <br /><em>Maiorana.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">I’m Tony—a chemist, medical device reviewer, and the writer behind <strong>The Polymerist.</strong> I’m interested in what it takes to turn good science into something useful.</p>
        <div class="hero-links"><a class="text-link" href="/about/">A little about me <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a><a class="text-link" href="/writing/">Explore the writing <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div>
        <p class="coordinates">Based in Washington, DC · Curious well beyond it</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="notebook" aria-labelledby="notebook-heading">
        <div class="notebook-top"><p class="eyebrow">An open notebook</p><span aria-hidden="true">№ 01</span></div>
        <h2 id="notebook-heading">On the workbench</h2>
        <ul class="notebook-list">
          <li><a href={site.leanLab}><span class="small-index">01</span><span>From research to a real product<small>The Lean Lab · Published guide</small></span><span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/projects/personal-website/"><span class="small-index">02</span><span>Building this digital workshop<small>AI-assisted website · In development</small></span><span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/ideas/"><span class="small-index">03</span><span>Questions worth following<small>Ideas & explorations</small></span><span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="notebook-note">A place for finished work,<br />and the next good question.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>
    <div class="intro-strip"><p class="eyebrow">Different fields.<br />Connected questions.</p><p><strong>From molecules to manufacturing</strong>Polymers, materials, and product development.</p><p><strong>From evidence to decisions</strong>Medical devices, technical evaluation, and risk.</p></div>
    <section class="section writing-grid" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
      <div class="publication-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Independent writing</p><h2 id="writing-heading">The <br />Polymerist<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></h2><p>Chemistry, industry, and the work of making new things possible. Written for people who want to understand what happens beyond the lab.</p><a class="text-link" href="/writing/">Explore the publication <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div>
      <div><ArticleList items={writing.items.filter(i => !i.url.includes('a-world-beyond-crude')).slice(0,3)} compact /><div class="section-link-row"><span class="meta">Selected from the publication</span><a class="text-link" href={site.polymerist}>Read on Substack <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="projects-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Learning by building</p><h2 id="projects-heading">Things in progress.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">The project notebook <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div><ProjectList /></section>
    <section class="section content-grid" aria-labelledby="research-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / The scientific record</p></div><div><h2 id="research-heading">The work underneath.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin:20px 0 26px;max-width:690px">Research on biobased epoxy resins, polymer nanocomposites, and materials. Industry work in adhesives and specialty chemicals. A career spent asking how things work—and whether they work well enough.</p><a class="text-link" href="/publications/">Publications & patents <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div></section>
    <section class="contact-band"><div><h2>What are you working on?</h2><p>Good questions tend to lead to good conversations.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
